{
  "id": "upstream-major-release-not-the-pr",
  "title": "CSV export tests fail inside the PR's function, but the cause is csvforge 3.0.0 (unpinned)",
  "description": "PR #77 adds a --since filter: it edits write_report() in src/reportcli/export.py (new filter_since() helper, new 'since' parameter) and adds tests. Four CSV tests fail, including the PR's new one, all with \"TypeError: write_rows() got an unexpected keyword argument 'header'\", and pytest's traceback points into write_report(), the function the PR changed, which invites blaming the PR. But the failing call, csvforge.write_rows(..., header=COLUMNS, ...), is unchanged (it sits outside the PR's hunk and is identical on main); pyproject.toml pins csvforge only as '>=2.4' and there is no lock file, so this install resolved the new major release csvforge 3.0.0 (shown in the pip output); and the test job on main has failed on its last two runs, on commits without this PR, after passing before. JSON tests pass. Correct answer: dependency (upstream breaking release), flaky=false: pin csvforge<3 in pyproject.toml or migrate the call to the 3.x API, independently of this PR.",
  "repo": {
    "owner": "example-org",
    "repo": "report-cli"
